      "writtenOn": "2021-06-28T18:39:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "My understanding is the BC1.2 is independent of USB-C.  BC1.2 only connects to USB2.0  D+ and D- signals for detection and advertisement.  The intersection with USB-C is only that BC1.2 is the fall back for charging when a non PD charger or device is connected.  Most accurate is to say \"BC1.2 charger detector/advertiser used on USB ports.\"  The port need not be USB-C nor dual-role.  Although it would be wasteful to use the PI3USB9201 on a dedicated USB host/device connection.",
      "parentUuid": "021215ea_5ad27c30",
